{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 132 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D9"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the sodium acetate shortage on 2016-02-03 and it remains current as of 2026-10-21, spanning 129 months on the list.",
      "cites": ["E40", "D13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The shortage posting names Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc., Hospira, Inc., Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC, Milla Pharmaceuticals, and Somerset Therapeutics, LLC as affected companies.",
      "cites": ["E36", "E37", "E35", "E38", "E39"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira's U.S. plant (FEI 1021343) received OAI classifications in 2010 and 2011, and a Warning Letter on 2010-04-12, all years before the 2016 posting.",
      "cites": ["E11", "E13", "E15", "E20"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pfizer Healthcare India Private Limited (FEI 3008316085) was inspected on 2015-09-24 and classified VAI, 132 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D9", "E24"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That same India plant later received an OAI classification on 2019-09-06 and a Warning Letter on 2020-03-25, well after the initial posting.",
      "cites": ["E27", "E29"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 11.4 days of the 20 mL presentation and 16.5 days of the 50 mL presentation; Corvale General holds 22.1 and 19.5 days respectively.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3", "D2", "D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-identified best option is to buy from Amneal Pharmaceuticals Private Limited, which is not on FDA's shortage list today, though its label names no plant we could place.",
      "cites": ["D14"]
    }
  ]
}
